{id:'itc',name:'ITC',ticker:'ITC',sector:'Everyday essentials',initial:'ITC',color:'#24407d',bg:'#eaf0fc',tag:'Look beyond the familiar brand',summary:'Foods, personal care and stationery sit alongside tobacco, paper and agricultural businesses.',description:'ITC operates across consumer goods, paperboards and packaging, agriculture and information technology. Its familiar food brands are only one part of the company.',products:[['Aashirvaad','Packaged foods'],['Sunfeast','Biscuits'],['Classmate','Stationery'],['Bingo!','Packaged snacks']],money:'Consumer purchases support its packaged-goods businesses, while other divisions sell products and services to business customers. Study tobacco and other consumer goods separately before assessing group performance.',ownership:'This page covers ITC Limited. A food brand associated with ITC does not represent the entire business. Check the current group structure and financial reports when comparing different periods.',watch:[['Segment profit','Which activities contribute earnings, rather than just sales?'],['Consumer-goods margins','Can newer categories cover manufacturing, distribution and advertising costs?'],['Cash generation','How much of reported profit turns into operating cash?']],risks:[['Tobacco regulation','Taxes and restrictions can affect the economics of the tobacco business.'],['Commodity exposure','Agricultural inputs and paper-related costs can fluctuate.'],['Brand competition','Building food and personal-care brands requires sustained investment.']],sources:[['ITC business profile','https://itcportal.com/about-itc/our-profile.html'],['Packaged foods portfolio','https://itcportal.com/itc-businesses/fmcg/food.html']],update:['Check the full business mix','ITC’s official profile covers businesses beyond its packaged-food brands. Compare those activities separately.'],question:'Can you judge ITC by the popularity of one biscuit brand?',answer:'No. A familiar brand is only part of a diversified company. The profit and risks of its other businesses also matter.'},
{id:'nestle-india',name:'Nestlé India',ticker:'NESTLEIND',sector:'Everyday essentials',initial:'N',color:'#75553d',bg:'#f6efe7',tag:'From the kitchen to the company',summary:'The Indian food and beverage business behind MAGGI, NESCAFÉ and MILKMAID.',description:'Nestlé India manufactures and sells food and beverage products under established brands. Its customers encounter the products in retail stores and other sales channels.',products:[['MAGGI','Prepared foods'],['NESCAFÉ','Coffee'],['MILKMAID','Milk products'],['KITKAT','Confectionery']],money:'It earns sales from packaged food and beverages. Revenue growth can come from selling more, changing prices or selling a different mix of products.',ownership:'Nestlé India Limited is the Indian listed company. The worldwide Nestlé group has a broader portfolio; global brand ownership does not imply that every global product is sold by Nestlé India.',watch:[['Sales volume','Is demand growing beyond the effect of price changes?'],['Input costs','How are coffee, milk and other ingredient costs changing?'],['Distribution','Can products reach more customers while remaining profitable?']],risks:[['Food quality','Quality problems can damage trust and disrupt sales.'],['Ingredient inflation','Higher costs may be difficult to pass on to customers.'],['Consumer preferences','Changes in tastes and spending affect product demand.']],sources:[['Nestlé India at a glance','https://www.nestle.in/about-us/at-a-glance'],['Coffee portfolio','https://www.nestle.in/brands/coffee'],['Q2 FY 2025–26 company release','https://www.nestle.in/sites/g/files/pydnoa451/files/2025-10/PressReleaseQ2FY2025-26.pdf']],update:['Read India-specific disclosures','Use the Indian company’s releases when researching these shares; global group results cover a different business perimeter.'],question:'Is buying Nestlé India the same as owning the entire global Nestlé business?',answer:'No. Your shares are in the Indian listed entity. Its operations, financial results and ownership relationships must be evaluated separately.'},
{id:'britannia',name:'Britannia Industries',ticker:'BRITANNIA',sector:'Everyday essentials',initial:'B',color:'#b52d3c',bg:'#fff0f1',tag:'A familiar place to begin',summary:'A packaged-food company whose products range from biscuits to bread and dairy.',description:'Britannia sells packaged foods across biscuits, dairy, bread, rusks, cakes and snacking. Recognisable brands help explain what shoppers buy, while the financial reports explain the business.',products:[['Good Day','Cookies'],['NutriChoice','Biscuits'],['Bourbon','Cream biscuits'],['Britannia dairy','Dairy products']],money:'Revenue comes from selling food products through its distribution channels. Ingredient prices, packaging, manufacturing and the mix of products sold affect earnings.',ownership:'The listed company is Britannia Industries Limited. Product brands are not separate listed stocks. Use consolidated disclosures when studying the group as a whole.',watch:[['Volume growth','Are consumers buying more packs?'],['Gross and operating margins','How much is left after ingredients and running costs?'],['Distribution reach','Can additional sales channels produce sustainable growth?']],risks:[['Ingredient costs','Wheat, sugar, milk and edible-oil prices can affect profitability.'],['Pricing pressure','Affordable alternatives limit how much prices can rise.'],['Execution','Expanding food categories and distribution costs money and requires consistent quality.']],sources:[['Britannia official portfolio','https://www.britannia.co.in/'],['NutriChoice range','https://www.britannia.co.in/product/nutrichoice'],['Good Day brand reference','https://www.britannia.co.in/article/talented-s-latest-for-britannia-good-day-doesn-t-show-the-biscuit-or-does-it']],update:['Explore beyond biscuits','The official product categories also include dairy, bread, rusk, cakes and snacking.'],question:'Why might a company sell more packs but earn less profit?',answer:'Ingredient costs, discounts, advertising or a shift toward cheaper products can offset the benefit of selling more.'},
{id:'marico',name:'Marico',ticker:'MARICO',sector:'Everyday essentials',initial:'m',color:'#177657',bg:'#e9f7ef',tag:'Brands hiding in plain sight',summary:'The consumer-goods business associated with Parachute, Saffola and Livon.',description:'Marico markets consumer products including coconut oils, edible oils, foods and personal-care products. The India brand directory is a useful starting point for connecting products to the company.',products:[['Parachute','Coconut oil'],['Saffola','Edible oils & foods'],['Livon','Hair care'],['Set Wet','Grooming']],money:'It earns money from consumer-product sales. Pricing, demand, product mix and the cost of ingredients influence the earnings left after operating expenses.',ownership:'This profile covers Marico Limited. Brand relationships can include different commercial arrangements; use the company’s own brand directory rather than assuming all associations mean full ownership.',watch:[['Volume growth','How much growth comes from increased consumption?'],['Commodity costs','What is happening to key oil and ingredient prices?'],['New categories','Are newer brands adding profitable sales?']],risks:[['Input volatility','Oil and ingredient costs can move sharply.'],['Brand dependence','Weakness in an important category can affect overall performance.'],['Expansion costs','New categories can require advertising before they earn meaningful profit.']],sources:[['Marico India brand directory','https://marico.com/india/brands']],update:['Check the brand relationship','Marico’s directory distinguishes some commercial rights from straightforward ownership. Read the relationship before mapping a brand.'],question:'Does a company marketing a brand always mean it owns that brand?',answer:'No. A company may have sales, distribution or licensing rights. The specific commercial relationship matters.'},
{id:'asian-paints',name:'Asian Paints',ticker:'ASIANPAINT',sector:'Homes & mobility',initial:'ap',color:'#854ba8',bg:'#f3ecf9',tag:'A business behind your walls',summary:'Paints and finishes that connect home improvement with a manufacturing business.',description:'Asian Paints offers paint products across different surfaces, finishes and price points. Its ranges give homeowners and painters choices for decorating and protecting surfaces.',products:[['Royale','Interior paints'],['Apcolite','Paints & finishes'],['Tractor','Economy paints'],['Trucare','Preparation products']],money:'Sales depend on painting demand, product selection and distribution. Manufacturing and selling higher-value products can change earnings, but so can raw-material and marketing costs.',ownership:'Asian Paints Limited is the listed company covered here. Individual product ranges such as Royale and Tractor are part of its offering, not separate listed companies.',watch:[['Volume growth','Is the quantity of paint sold increasing?'],['Product mix','Are customers choosing premium or economy products?'],['Operating margin','Can the company defend profit while competing on price and service?']],risks:[['Competition','New capacity and competing brands can put pressure on pricing and dealer relationships.'],['Input costs','Ingredients and packaging influence manufacturing costs.'],['Painting demand','Home improvement can be postponed when household budgets tighten.']],sources:[['Tractor paint and related ranges','https://www.asianpaints.com/paint-products/interior-wall-paints/plain-finishes/tractor-emulsion.html'],['Official investor product presentation','https://www.asianpaints.com/content/dam/asianpaints/website/secondary-navigation/investors/analyst-presentations-2/2024-2025/InvestorsPresentation_PDF_copy.pdf']],update:['Distinguish products from performance','The product catalogue explains the offering. Financial reports are needed to establish the current sales and earnings mix.'],question:'Does a premium paint selling at a higher price guarantee higher company profit?',answer:'No. Production costs, selling expenses, discounts and the amount sold also influence profit.'},
{id:'maruti-suzuki',name:'Maruti Suzuki India',ticker:'MARUTI',sector:'Homes & mobility',initial:'M',color:'#24569a',bg:'#eaf3fd',tag:'From the road to the business',summary:'Passenger vehicles, sales channels and services built around car ownership.',description:'Maruti Suzuki India sells vehicles through its ARENA and NEXA channels and provides related ownership services. Its website also covers commercial vehicles, parts and accessories.',products:[['Swift','Passenger car'],['Ertiga','Passenger vehicle'],['NEXA','Sales channel'],['Genuine parts','Vehicle parts']],money:'Selling vehicles is central to the business. Unit sales, the type of vehicles sold, discounts and production costs help explain changes in earnings.',ownership:'This profile covers Maruti Suzuki India Limited. ARENA and NEXA are sales channels, not independent listed car manufacturers. Do not confuse the Indian entity with the worldwide Suzuki group.',watch:[['Unit sales','Separate the number of vehicles sold from their selling prices.'],['Vehicle mix','Different models and categories have different economics.'],['Capacity use','Factories need sufficient demand to use investments efficiently.']],risks:[['Purchase cycles','Cars are large purchases that customers may defer.'],['Competition','Rival models and discounts can affect demand and margins.'],['Production costs','Materials, components and investment needs influence cash generation.']],sources:[['Maruti Suzuki corporate and vehicle site','https://www.marutisuzuki.com/'],['Vehicle directory','https://www.marutisuzuki.com/sitemap']],update:['Use the right sales channel','The official site separates ARENA, NEXA and other channels. A channel name is different from a vehicle brand or legal entity.'],question:'Why is the number of cars sold not enough to explain revenue?',answer:'Different models sell at different prices. Revenue also depends on the mix, discounts and other sales.'},
{id:'bajaj-auto',name:'Bajaj Auto',ticker:'BAJAJ-AUTO',sector:'Homes & mobility',initial:'BA',color:'#246091',bg:'#eaf4fc',tag:'Two wheels, several businesses',summary:'Motorcycles, electric scooters and commercial vehicles for different kinds of journeys.',description:'Bajaj Auto’s product portfolio includes motorcycles, scooters and three-wheelers. Its official site lists ranges including Pulsar and Chetak.',products:[['Pulsar','Motorcycles'],['Chetak','Electric scooters'],['Dominar','Motorcycles'],['Three-wheelers','Commercial vehicles']],money:'The company earns revenue from selling vehicles and related products. Vehicle type, selling price, market demand and manufacturing costs affect performance.',ownership:'Bajaj Auto Limited is the listed vehicle business covered here. Other Bajaj-named financial and consumer businesses are separate listed entities or group companies.',watch:[['Volume and mix','How are motorcycle, scooter and commercial-vehicle sales changing?'],['Market demand','Are sales broad-based across the markets served?'],['Margins','How do materials, pricing and new technologies affect profit?']],risks:[['Demand cycles','Customers may postpone replacing vehicles.'],['Technology transition','Electric mobility requires investment and creates new competition.'],['Market exposure','Economic conditions in different sales markets can affect demand.']],sources:[['Bajaj Auto product portfolio','https://www.bajajauto.com/'],['FY 2025–26 management discussion','https://investors.bajajauto.com/ar26/management-discussion-analysis/']],update:['Read the vehicle mix','The FY 2025–26 management discussion provides context beyond a single popular model.'],question:'Does owning Bajaj Auto mean you directly own every Bajaj business?',answer:'No. Shares represent ownership in a specific legal entity. Related names do not make separate companies interchangeable.'},
{id:'bharti-airtel',name:'Bharti Airtel',ticker:'BHARTIARTL',sector:'Technology & services',initial:'a',color:'#bf2e34',bg:'#fff0ef',tag:'The business behind your connection',summary:'Mobile connections, home internet and enterprise connectivity sold as recurring services.',description:'Bharti Airtel provides telecommunications and digital services. Its portfolio includes mobile, home broadband, television and connectivity for enterprise customers.',products:[['Airtel mobile','Mobile connectivity'],['Airtel Wi-Fi','Home broadband'],['Digital TV','Television services'],['Airtel Business','Enterprise connectivity']],money:'Customers pay for connectivity and related services. Subscriber numbers and average spending matter alongside the cost of operating and expanding the network.',ownership:'This profile covers Bharti Airtel Limited. Group structure and geography matter: the listed company is broader than a single Indian mobile plan.',watch:[['Revenue per user','How much does the average customer pay for service?'],['Customer base','Are users joining, staying and choosing higher-value plans?'],['Network investment','How much cash is needed to maintain and expand service?']],risks:[['Competition','Pricing and customer retention depend partly on competitors.'],['Capital needs','Networks require substantial continuing investment.'],['Regulation','Telecom obligations and spectrum costs affect business economics.']],sources:[['Bharti Airtel business overview','https://www.airtel.in/about-bharti/about-bharti-airtel/'],['FY 2024–25 annual report','https://www.airtel.in/airtel-annual-report-2024-25/']],update:['Read services and geography together','The business includes consumer and enterprise services. The linked annual report covers FY 2024–25 and is historical, not the latest quarter.'],question:'Can revenue grow without adding more subscribers?',answer:'Yes. Average spending can rise as customers change plans or buy additional services. Customer count and spending should be read together.'},
{id:'hdfc-bank',name:'HDFC Bank',ticker:'HDFCBANK',sector:'Banking',initial:'H',color:'#244776',bg:'#ebf0f8',tag:'Understanding a different business model',summary:'A bank connecting deposits, lending, payments and services for people and businesses.',description:'HDFC Bank offers accounts, deposits, loans, cards and banking services to personal and business customers. Its product directory illustrates both lending and transaction services.',products:[['Savings accounts','Deposits & payments'],['Home loans','Housing finance'],['Credit cards','Credit & payments'],['Business banking','Services for companies']],money:'A bank earns interest on loans and other earning assets, while paying interest on funding. It also earns fees. Credit losses and operating expenses affect how much becomes profit.',ownership:'The listed entity is HDFC Bank Limited. A financial product distributed by the bank is not automatically manufactured by it; check the provider and the specific group relationship.',watch:[['Net interest margin','How much net interest does the bank earn relative to earning assets?'],['Bad loans','Are borrowers keeping up with payments?'],['Deposit growth','Can the bank attract funding at a sustainable cost?']],risks:[['Credit losses','Borrowers may fail to repay loans.'],['Funding costs','Paying more for deposits can reduce interest margins.'],['Operational risk','Service disruptions and control failures can hurt customers and the business.']],sources:[['HDFC Bank business overview','https://www.hdfc.bank.in/about-us/our-businesses']],update:['Banking needs different measures','Compare lending, funding and credit quality together. A bank’s financial statements should not be read like a packaged-food company’s.'],question:'Is the money customers deposit into a bank the bank’s revenue?',answer:'No. A deposit is money the bank owes the customer. Interest and fees earned are different from customer deposit balances.'}
